{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "warming": true,
  "agents": {
    "explore": {
      "model": "claude-agent/haiku"
    },
    "general": {
      "model": "opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash"
    },
    "ui-implementer": {
      "description": "Implements the UI/UX part of one ticket slice in a given worktree, following the repo's UI guidance.",
      "mode": "subagent",
      "model": "claude-agent/opus",
      "variant": "high",
      "system": "You implement exactly the UI/UX part of one ticket slice in the worktree you are given, and nothing else.\n\nRules:\n- Follow the repo's AGENTS.md and its coding conventions.\n- Stay inside the given worktree and the ticket's scope.\n- Commit through the git hooks. Never use --no-verify, never force-push, never rebase pushed work.\n- Do not add new unit or integration tests.\n- When done, report the files you changed, the commits you made, and any decisions or assumptions you made.\n\nUI/UX work:\n- Before any UI work, find and follow the repo's UI guidance: AGENTS.md and any docs it links for screens, components, styling or design systems. Use the repo's component library and design tokens; never introduce ad-hoc colors, fonts or one-off styles.\n- Design mobile (390x844) and desktop (1440x900) properly, with accessible labels, focus states, and empty/loading/error states.\n- Also report the components used or added, and any custom component and why."
    },
    "tester": {
      "description": "Tests the running app by hand: web apps with the browse MCP, mobile and desktop apps with agent-device. Reports pass/fail per acceptance criterion with screenshot and video proof. Never edits code.",
      "mode": "subagent",
      "model": "openai/gpt-6.1-terra#medium",
      "system": "You are the QA tester. You verify; you never edit code.\n\nRules:\n- Test only with these two tools: the `browse` MCP for web apps, and the `agent-device` MCP for mobile (iOS, Android) and desktop apps. You may also use the `executor` MCP for supporting data and services (such as reading tickets or inboxes), never to drive the app. Never use agent-desktop, the built-in app browser, Playwright, or any other browser or device tool.\n- Drive the running app by hand against each acceptance criterion. There is no scripted browser harness (verify-herder was removed, Jose, Nov 10 2026): never write or run browser test scripts or journeys.\n- Check every acceptance criterion you are given and report pass or fail per AC, with evidence: screenshot file paths and the steps you took.\n- Use Mailpit to read email codes.\n- Do not edit code or files in the repo. If something fails, report it with evidence and stop. PROOF (Jose, Nov 9 2026): For every acceptance criterion, capture visual proof at both mobile (390x844) and desktop (1440x900) viewports. Before each pass, use browse `execute` with `await page.setViewportSize({ width, height })`. Save one screenshot per AC per viewport under `~/.cache/herder-build/proof/<issue-key-lowercase>/` (e.g. `ac1-mobile.png`, `ac1-desktop.png`) via `page.screenshot({ path })` or `screenshotWithLabels({ path })` (absolute paths under that proof dir; OPENCODE_BROWSER_FILE_ROOTS includes it). Also record one short video per viewport that walks the ticket's main journey: call the browse MCP `recording` tool with action `start` (prefer mode `cdp`, `outputPath` ending in `.mp4` under the same proof dir, e.g. `journey-mobile.mp4` / `journey-desktop.mp4`), run the journey, then `recording` action `stop`. Do not read browser profiles, cookies, or saved sessions. Do not upload to Google Drive. Return every screenshot and video absolute path in the test report, keyed by AC and viewport. A report missing screenshots or videos for either viewport is incomplete — mark the run failed. NATIVE APP PROOF: For mobile and desktop apps tested with agent-device, save one screenshot per AC per device with the agent-device `screenshot` tool, and record one short video of the main journey per device with the agent-device `record` tool (start before the journey, stop after). Save them under the same proof dir, named like `ac1-ios.png`, `ac1-android.png`, `ac1-macos.png` and `journey-ios.mp4`. Test every platform the ticket targets. Return every path in the report, keyed by AC and device; a report missing them is incomplete — mark the run failed. LOGIN THROTTLE (Jose, Nov 9 2026): Clear the login rate limit yourself instead of sleeping or waiting out the 10-minute login-code window. You may delete only `auth_throttle` rows whose key matches `ip:127.0.0.1:%`, and only on the ticket's own Neon branch `ticket-<issue>` or on dev (project calm-dawn-32120207, branch br-nameless-credit-b8xhp96i). Never prod or main, never any other branch, table, or rows. Log every clear (time, branch, rows deleted) in `~/.cache/herder-build/throttle-clears.log`. Use the database connection the process already gets through its process-only env override, or the repo's Neon helpers (`scripts/lib/neon-api.ts` + `herder-neon.ts`). Prefer `~/.cache/herder-orchestrator/clear-login-throttle.sh <issue>` when a ticket Neon branch is in use — it is already scoped and writes the log. Never edit Doppler or print secrets.",
      "permissions": [
        {
          "action": "browse_*",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "allow"
        },
        {
          "action": "agent-device_*",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "allow"
        },
        {
          "action": "executor_*",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "allow"
        },
        {
          "action": "rea_*",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "deny"
        },
        {
          "action": "agent-desktop_*",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "deny"
        },
        {
          "action": "edit",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "deny"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "instructions": [
    "DESIGN.md"
  ],
  "mcp": {
    "servers": {
      "rea": {
        "type": "local",
        "command": [
          "npx",
          "-y",
          "rea-agents@6.9.0",
          "mcp"
        ],
        "disabled": false,
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" }}
        "environment": {
          "HOPPER_LAUNCHER_PATH": "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/Applications/Hopper Disassembler.app/Contents/MacOS/hopper"
        }
{{- end }}
      },
      "firecrawl": {
        "type": "remote",
        "url": "https://mcp.firecrawl.dev/v2/mcp-oauth"
      },
      "executor": {
        "type": "remote",
        "url": "https://mcp.executor.sh/mcp?connection=995a9bc9-b256-4404-b4a7-48db88e9df51"
      },
      "browse": {
        "type": "local",
        "command": [
          "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.local/bin/browse",
          "mcp"
        ],
        "environment": {
          "OPENCODE_BROWSER_RUNTIME": "auto-update",
          "OPENCODE_BROWSER_FILE_ROOTS": "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.cache/herder-build/proof"
        },
        "cwd": "~",
        "pool": true
      },
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" }}
      "agent-desktop": {
        "type": "local",
        "command": [
          "/opt/homebrew/bin/agent-desktop",
          "mcp"
        ]
      },
{{- end }}
      "agent-device": {
        "type": "local",
        "command": [
          "npx",
          "-y",
          "agent-device@0.21.37",
          "mcp"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "providers": {
    "openai": {
      "settings": {
        "compaction": {
          "type": "native"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "experimental": {
    "background_compaction": true
  },
  "shell": "/bin/bash",
  "default_agent": "build",
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "linux" }}
  // OpenCode is installed and updated by mise on Linux.
  "update": "disable",
{{- end }}
  "plugins": [
    "./plugins/tokeneconomizer",
    "opencode-mobile-notifications",
    "@honcho-ai/opencode-honcho",
    "-local.agent-memory-repo"
  ]
}
